QuestGuidance.Register("en",374,{
[11937]="70028D50\n1\tTalk to Myve in Galtrev about the missing toy\tMyve, the child who seemed to covet the shiny toy, is somewhere in Galtrev. You should speak with Myve to see if she is hiding the shiny ball from its rightful owner.\n2\tSearch Galtrev for someone with information about the toy ball\tSomeone who may have witnessed the pilfering of Envus's toy would likely be in Galtrev. You should look around and see if anyone saw someone make off with the shiny ball.\n3\tFind the crow that stole the child's toy ball\tThe crow that stole the ball was seen flying to the north-west. You should head north-west to try and recover Envus' favourite toy.\n",
[11938]="70066930\n1\tMiruhir has asked you to shoo away birds that are eating valuable wine grapes at his vineyard in Iáphel. Shoo away birds.\t\n2\tTalk to Miruhir\tYou should tell Miruhir that you have shooed the birds away. Miruhir can be found in Iáphel.\n",
[11939]="70062610\n1\tDiscover the lost towers of Caranost\tThough now crumbling, the towers of Caranost once watched over the land for miles and miles.\n2\tDiscover the eastern tower\030Discover the south-western tower\030Discover the central tower\030Discover the north-western tower\tYou should discover the crumbling towers of Caranost. Caranost is in western Cardolan.\n",
[11940]="70061179\n1\tSearch the abandoned burrows\tThe abandoned burrows of Glynafon are in the eastern Angle. You should explore the abandoned burrows and bring anything of interest back to Cedivor.\n2\tShow the stone to Cedivor\tCedivor Hedgerow is outside of Glynafon, in the eastern Angle. You should bring the stone to Cedivor.\n3\tBring the stone to Narnien\tNarnien is located in Gaerond, in the northern Angle. You should tell Narnien that you have found a strange artifact.\n",
[11941]="70067C38\n1\tYou discovered a note on the body of the Haradrim sorcerer. You cannot make any sense of the symbols used on the note but can reason that it is writing of some type. This is likely something that Girgish should see. Return it to her at Jax Phanâl.\t\n",
[11942]="700588A4\n1\tCollect the first page\030Collect the second page\030Collect the third page\030Collect the fourth page\030Collect the fifth page\030Collect the sixth page\030Collect the seventh page\030Collect the eighth page\030Collect the ninth page\030Collect the tenth page\030Collect the new journal\tLost pages from the Crystal Journal can be found across Elderslade. You should look for more pages from the Crystal Journal.\n2\tBring your findings to Mother Amma\tFrom across the wasted lands of Elderslade you have gathered the missing pages of the Crystal Journal, as well as the sorceress' new records. Bring your findings to Mother Amma in the forge at Annâk-khurfu.\n",
[11943]="70033125\n1\tDefeat Ghâsh-hai Orcs at Hurmulkezer\tGhâsh-hai Orcs can be found at Hurmulkezer, south of Durin's Court at the south-eastern edge of the Flaming Deeps. You should defeat Orcs at Hurmulkezer.\n2\tDefeat Ghâsh-hai Orcs at Hurmulkezer (total: 8)\tGhâsh-hai Orcs can be found at Hurmulkezer, south of Durin's Court at the south-eastern edge of the Flaming Deeps. You should defeat Orcs at Hurmulkezer.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have defeated a number of the Ghâsh-hai Orcs at Hurmulkezer, weakening their forces and assuring that they will no longer pose a threat.\n",
[11944]="70048C70\n1\tTalk to Faeron\tFaeron can be found in Viznak's hideout. You should talk to Faeron about Viznak's proposition.\n2\tTalk to Viznak\tViznak can be found in his hideout. You should talk to Viznak.\n3\tCollect infected livers (total: 5)\030Collect Plague Mushrooms (total: 5)\030Collect swamp water (quantity: see journal)\030Collect infected insect guts (total: 5)\tViznak has provided a list of ingredients that can be found in the wilds of Agarnaith. Infected livers can be collected from gore-crows, wolves, boars, and rats. Infected insect guts can be collected from sickle-flies, nerbyg, and swarming flies. You should collect infected livers, plague mushrooms, swamp water, and infected insect guts.\n4\tMix disgusting concoction in mixing bowl\tViznak mentioned he had a mixing bowl in his hideout. You should mix the ingredients together in the mixing bowl.\n5\tDrink the disgusting concoction\tThe disgusting concoction has been created and awaits you in Viznak's hideout. You should bravely attempt to ingest the disgusting concoction.\n6\tTalk to Faeron\030Help Rhadrog take the concoction\tFaeron and Rhadrog can be found in Viznak's hideout. You should give the disgusting concoction to both of the Rangers.\n7\tTalk to Viznak\tViznak can be found in his hideout. You should talk to Viznak.\n",
[11945]="7007179D\n1\tBurn saplings (total: 6)\030Raze ground (total: 4)\tTálbiral has asked that you raze the ground surrounding Laivárth and any blighted saplings you encounter to prevent the spread from getting closer to the grove.\n2\tReturn to Tálbiral in Laivárth\tTálbiral will want to know that you successfully removed the saplings and razed the ground again. Return to him in Laivárth.\n",
[11946]="7004E9E4\n1\tDwarf-wights can be found within Thikil-gundu. Nori has asked you to seek out\t\n2\tReturn to Thikil-gundu and complete 'In Death's Grasp'\t\n",
[11947]="70067CB4\n1\tSpeak with the shade\tA shade of a dead Corsair begged for help in finding peace.\n2\tCollect the stolen gold\tThe shade wants you to find his body, collect the stolen treasure, and return the gold to the chest. The shade believes that this will set him free.\n3\tReturn to the treasure cache and restore the treasure\tThe shade reappeared and warned that you must return the treasure to the chest or suffer the same fate. Return to the open chest in the salamander grotto and restore the treasure.\n4\tTalk to Jeduth the Cursed\tThe treasure is whole, and the shade remains. It seems to beckon to you.\n",
[11948]="70047BE9\n1\tAttempt to approach the hill-top of Dol Acharn\tDol Acharn can be found in eastern Dagorlad. Faramir has asked you to approach the hill to confirm his suspicions about the Wainriders. You should scout the hill carefully.\n2\tTalk to Faramir near Dol Acharn\tFaramir can be found due west of Dol Acharn in Dagorlad. You attempted to reach the hill-top of Dol Acharn but found your efforts repelled by an unseen force that sapped your will to press onward. You should return to Faramir and tell him of what you have experienced.\n",
[11949]="700544D6\n1\tDefeat the Cursed Rider in Mordor Besieged\tHe moved at speed across the battlefield, running down the warriors who dared stand against him, fewer as the siege went on. He was the Cursed Rider, and the sound of his approach turned even courageous blood to water. In later years he would command armies from within the walls of Dol Guldur, but during the Second Age he preferred to fight from the back of his black steed, alone.\n2\tDefeat the Cursed Rider in Mordor Besieged\tHe moved at speed across the battlefield, running down the warriors who dared stand against him, fewer as the siege went on. He was the Cursed Rider, and the sound of his approach turned even courageous blood to water. In later years he would command armies from within the walls of Dol Guldur, but during the Second Age he preferred to fight from the back of his black steed, alone.\n3\tThe Cursed Rider, defeated but enduring\tHe moved at speed across the battlefield, running down the warriors who dared stand against him, fewer as the siege went on. He was the Cursed Rider, and the sound of his approach turned even courageous blood to water. In later years he would command armies from within the walls of Dol Guldur, but during the Second Age he preferred to fight from the back of his black steed, alone.\n",
[11950]="700494CE\n1\tDefeat the lesser shades of the watching stone (quantity: see journal)\tThe watching stone can be found in Talath Úrui. You should defeat the watching stone's shades.\n2\tConfront the watching stone\tThe watching stone can be found in Talath Úrui. You should confront the watching stone.\n",
[11951]="70040432\n1\tTalk to Malthellam in Morlad\tMalthellam can be found outside his home in Morlad in north-western Blackroot Vale. You have been urged to return to Malthellam by Gordir, who hopes that your experiences in Alagrant and Sardol will goad the Steward into taking action.\n2\tTalk to Malthellam\tMalthellam can be found in Morlad, outside his home. Malthellam has asked you to speak with him and Rosfin about what you encountered in Alagrant and Sardol.\n3\tTalk to Rosfin\tLady Rosfin can be found outside Malthellam's home in Morlad. You have finished speaking with Lady Rosfin and Malthellam about the threats you encountered in the south, and should now speak to Rosfin.\n",
[11952]="7004BEAC\n1\tCollect sûlok feed from the feed bag\tA feed bag can be found in Fushaum Bal North. You should collect sûlok feed from the feed bag.\n2\tSûlokil can be found in Fushaum Bal North. You should feed the sûlokil.\t\n3\tTalk to the Khundolar Commander\tThe Khundolar Commander can be found at Fushaum Bal North. You should talk to the Khundolar Commander.\n",
[11953]="70062AA9\n1\tMake it to the marked spot on the edge of the Wadewater without running out of time\tAlla has given you five minutes to reach the spot in question on the edge of the Wadewater, north of Mossward. This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n2\tReturn to Alla in north-eastern Mossward without running out of time\tAlla is by a haystack in north-eastern Mossward. You only have five minutes for the return journey! This stage includes failure conditions; check the journal before choosing objects or actions.\n3\tTalk to Alla in north-eastern Mossward\tAlla is by a haystack in north-eastern Mossward.\n",
[11954]="7001AD23\n1\tDefeat Mâb Rhûnadan\030Destroy the corrupted altar\tMâb Rhûnadan and his altar may be found at Sâd Morangol. Ianudirel has asked you to destroy the altar of Mâb Rhûnadan or defeat the Cargûl himself.\n2\tTalk to Ianudirel\tIanudirel is just south of the bridge at Krul Lugu. You should return to Ianudirel with news of your success.\n",
[11955]="7004A3A3\n1\tApproach Anglach\tYou should approach the great forges of Anglach in Udûn, and search for a way in.\n2\tSearch for Lachír in Anglach\tSearch for Captain Lachír and his men within the great forges of Anglach, in Udûn.\n3\tSearch for Lachír in Anglach\tSearch for Captain Lachír and his men within the great forges of Anglach, in Udûn.\n4\tSearch for Lachír in Anglach\tSearch for Captain Lachír and his men within the great forges of Anglach, in Udûn.\n5\tSearch for Lachír in Anglach\tSearch for Captain Lachír and his men within the great forges of Anglach, in Udûn.\n6\tFind Lachír\tFollow the voices of Men within the great forges of Anglach, in Udûn.\n7\tTalk to Captain Lachír\tYou should talk to Captain Lachír now that you have found him in the lower levels of Anglach, in Udûn.\n",
[11956]="700479D1\n1\tCollect phials of viscous poison (total: 5)\030Collect phials of refined poison (total: 8)\tPhials of poison can be found on Uruks and Orcs in Cair Andros. You should collect phials of poison.\n2\tStudy the phials of refined poison at Henneth Annûn\tA workbench can be found at Henneth Annûn. You should bring the phials of poison to Henneth Annûn for study.\n3\tStudy the phials of viscous poison at Henneth Annûn\tA workbench can be found at Henneth Annûn. You should bring the phials of poison to Henneth Annûn for study.\n4\tSpeak with Mílgamel\tMílgamel can be found at Henneth Annûn. You should take the poisons and what you have learned to her.\n",
[11957]="700494CD\n1\tDefeat Darkwaters at Ashronk (total: 3)\030Defeat Darkwaters at Krulronk (total: 3)\030Defeat Darkwaters at Gakhronk (total: 3)\030Defeat Darkwaters at Zagronk (total: 3)\tDarkwaters can be found in pools around Talath Úrui. You should defeat Darkwaters gathered at each of the pools in Talath Úrui.\n2\tReturn to the watching stone\tThe watching stone can be found in Talath Úrui. You should return to the watching stone.\n",
[11958]="70041A49\n1\tTalk to the Night-jewel deckhand\tThe Night-jewel deckhand can be found on the shore of Barad Rill. Daxamat made landfall with his brethren at Barad Rill and then spoke to a deckhand.\n2\tEnter the lighthouse of Barad Rill\tThe lighthouse of Barad Rill can be found at the centre of the small shoal off the southern coast of Dor-en-Ernil. The deckhand has directed Daxamat to enter the lighthouse and speak to the Scourge at his request.\n3\tMeet the Scourge at the peak of Barad Rill\tThe peak of Barad Rill can be found by climbing the stairs in the ruin. Daxamat searched Barad Rill for Balakhôr and climbed toward the top of the ruin.\n4\tTalk to Balakhôr the Scourge\tBalakhôr can be found atop Barad Rill. Daxamat then went into Barad Rill to seek Balakhôr at the top.\n5\tObserve the meeting of the Black Blade and Balakhôr\tBalakhôr and the Black Blade of Lebennin can be found atop Barad Rill. Daxamar is describing the meeting between one of the Nine and Balakhôr. You should listen to his tale.\n",
[11959]="70041A4F\n1\tListen to Daxamat's recounting of his journey through Dor-en-Ernil\tDaxamat can be found in the northernmost part of Hata Kebir in eastern Lebennin. Daxamat has asked to share his account of an upsetting meeting he witnessed in Dor-en-Ernil. You should listen to his tale.\n2\tTalk to Daxamat in Hata Kebir\tDaxamat can be found in the northernmost part of Hata Kebir in eastern Lebennin. Daxamat has finished telling the tale of his encounter with the Black Blade of Lebennin. You should speak to him.\n",
[11960]="7004CF85\n1\tReturn to Caras Tilion\tRadagast has suggested that you should return to Caras Tilion, in the mountains on the southern border of Eryn Lasgalen.\n2\tFind where the Rhachló flows through Caras Tilion\tCaras Tilion can be found in the mountains on the southern border of Eryn Lasgalen. The Rhachló must flow through Caras Tilion.\n3\tSearch for artifacts (total: 8)\tCaras Tilion can be found in the mountains on the southern border of Eryn Lasgalen. Search Caras Tilion for dark artifacts.\n4\tContinue searching\tCaras Tilion can be found in the mountains on the southern border of Eryn Lasgalen. Search Caras Tilion for anything from Dol Guldur that isn't broken.\n5\tTalk to Radagast\tRadagast can be found at the tree nursery just outside of Felegoth. You should return to Radagast and tell him all that you saw in Caras Tilion.\n6\tTalk to Radagast\tRadagast can be found at the tree nursery just outside of Felegoth. You should return to Radagast and tell him all that you saw in Caras Tilion.\n",
[11961]="7004CF84\n1\tEnter Caras Tilion\tYou should investigate Caras Tilion, which can be found in the mountains at the southern edge of Eryn Lasgalen.\n2\tDefeat armoured shadows (total: 6)\030Defeat sorcerous spirits (total: 8)\030Explore the northern courtyard\030Explore the southern overlook\030Explore the eastern overlook\030Explore the central courtyard\tCaras Tilion can be found in the mountains at the southern edge of Eryn Lasgalen. You should investigate Caras Tilion and defeat any of the darkness within its crumbled walls.\n3\tReconvene with Oroniel\tHaving explored and dealt with the shadows, you should reconvene with Oroniel in Caras Tilion.\n4\tCome to Oroniel's aid\tYou should go quickly to Oroniel, where she called out for aid in Caras Tilion.\n",
[11962]="7004117F\n1\tDefeat Umbarrim sorcerers in Tarlang's Crown (total: 3)\tUmbarrim sorcerers can be found in Corsair encampments in Tarlang's Crown. Gondren has asked you to defeat Umbarrim sorcerers to prevent them from bringing forth any more fell spirits in Tarlang's Crown.\n2\tTalk to Harnion\tHarnion can be found along the road through Tarlang's Crown, to the north of Edhellond in Belfalas. You have defeated many Umbarrim sorcerers and stopped them from summoning more vile fell spirits into Gondor. You should now return to Harnion.\n",
[11963]="7005465D\n1\tDefeat Lhothbad\030Defeat Iárvereth\030Defeat Saeriel\tThe Daughters of Iphantemel are lurking somewhere in Taurlingol. You should defeat Lhothbad, Iárvereth, and Saeriel.\n2\tTalk to Legolas\tLegolas can be found on a hill near Taurlingol. You should talk to Legolas.\n",
[11964]="700346E5\n1\tListen to Gifemund's tale\tGifemund can be found at the refugees' hideout in the Whitshaws. You should talk to Gifemund to find out more about the refugees' story.\n2\tSpeak with Cyneberg\tCyneberg is at the refugees' hideout south-west of Dunfast. You should speak with Cyneberg.\n",
[11965]="70003277\n1\tBring \"The Lay of Nimrodel\" to Toronn at Celondim\tToronn is at Celondim, south of Duillond. Bregar has asked you to take the scroll to Toronn in the hope that it will convince his brother to remain.\n",
[11966]="700413CC\n1\tSpeak with Arvaethor\tArvaethor can be found in the village of Ethring in Ringló Vale. You should speak with Arvaethor.\n2\tDestroy the ominous standing stones (total: 4)\030Defeat Ruthless Dead in Ringló Vale (total: 6)\tStrange standing stones can be found north of the river Ringló. You should destroy any strange standing stones you find.\n3\tSpeak with Arvaethor\tArvaethor can be found near a mountain pass in the north-western part of Ringló Vale. You should speak with Arvaethor.\n",
[11967]="7006C136\n1\tSearch the grounds of Adakûr\tSearch the grounds of Adakûr near the crypts of Esh-kimâkhi for signs of the quartet of travellers.\n2\tDefeat crypt-guardians (total: 7)\030Defeat crypt-sentinels (total: 5)\030Defeat crypt-horrors (total: 3)\tDefeat the crypt-wights around you!\n3\tSearch the great tombs of Esh-kimâkhi for any sign of the final traveller\tSearch the great tombs of Esh-kimâkhi for any sign of the final traveller.\n4\tDefeat the dread-wight Adâru-guzi\tDefeat the dread-wight Adâru-guzi in Esh-kimâkhi.\n",
[11968]="70067F7E\n1\tSpeak with Othax\tYou were asked if you wanted to participate in a macabre game that the workers of Rakhatâb are playing. You will need to pay the entry fee and then make a choice: Which foreman do you think will have an accident befall a worker under their care?\n",
})
